# Web admin scope

Read `web/.cursor/plans/web-admin.md` before `web-admin` work. Follow the slice order. Do not start a later slice until the previous slice's checks exist.

When a slice's checks finish, write `web/.cursor/progress/<stage>/slice-<number>-<name>.md` before the next slice. Record what was done, what was tested and the result, any failure and why, and what is next.

Build only spec Section 10.1: login, System Admin activation, protected routes, role-aware navigation, admin accounts, student list and create, re-issue on a pending student, cookie-backed refresh, an OpenAPI-derived client, and Bangla plus English catalogs. Student registration, student activation, and password reset belong to `mobile`.

Before screen code, read `web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. This app is Next.js 16. Use `src/proxy.ts` exporting `proxy`. Do not add `middleware.ts`.

```tsx
// BAD — user-facing copy inline
<button>Create student</button>

// GOOD — catalog key, both locales
<button>{t("students.create")}</button>
```

A wrong API field or cookie is an `api` defect. Fix `api` and its tests before adapting the client around it.
